     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Each 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 850 mg to 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, for 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
